<h1>Results</h1>
This is a representative output for `mpirun -n 4 ./mpi-logger`. Because the ranks run concurrently, the exact
interleaving of the per-rank lines varies from run to run:

@code{.cpp}

Starting distributed solver apply (will trigger MPI events)...
[Rank 0] AllToAll started...
[Rank 1] AllToAll started...
[Rank 2] AllToAll started...
[Rank 3] AllToAll started...
[Rank 0] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 1] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 2] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 3] AllToAll completed.
[Rank 0] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
...
Distributed solver apply completed.
Starting distributed vector dot product (will trigger MPI all_reduce)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce started for 1 elements (8 bytes)...
[Rank 0] AllReduce completed for 1 elements (8 bytes).
Dot product result: 16
Starting point-to-point communication (send/recv)...
[Rank 0] Sending 1 elements (4 bytes) to Rank 1...
[Rank 0] Send to Rank 1 completed (4 bytes).
[Rank 1] Received value: 42
[Rank 1] Receiving 1 elements (4 bytes) from Rank 0...
[Rank 1] Recv from Rank 0 completed (4 bytes).
[Rank 1] Received non-blocking value: 43

@endcode

Each MPI operation issued through the logged communicator produces a matching <code>_started</code> /
<code>_completed</code> pair, tagged with the rank, the peer (for point-to-point and rooted collectives) and the
element/byte counts.
